  "hindi": "कल्याण देने वाला, जनों का स्वामी, वृत्र को मारने वाला, शत्रुओं को कुचलने वाला, वश में रखने वाला, बलवान् इन्द्र, सोम पीने वाला और अभय करने वाला, हमारे आगे-आगे चले।",
  "english": "Giver of well-being, lord of the clans, slayer of Vṛtra, scatterer of foes, the master, mighty Indra, drinker of Soma, maker of fearlessness, let him go before us.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "vṛṣā is read as an epithet 'bull, mighty' of Indra. The printed ḙ in etu is the letter e carrying a Vedic accent mark, not a typo. puraḥ etu is taken as 'let him go in front'.",
