  "hindi": "रक्षस् को चूर-चूर करो, शत्रुओं को चूर-चूर करो; वृत्र के दोनों जबड़े तोड़ डालो। हे वृत्रहन् इन्द्र, आक्रमण करने वाले शत्रु के क्रोध को तोड़ दो।",
  "english": "Strike the rakṣas apart, strike the foes apart; break apart the two jaws of Vṛtra. Break apart, Indra, slayer of Vṛtra, the wrath of the enemy who assails.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The verb ruja is understood with vi in line 2. rakṣaḥ is the harmful being (rakṣas), taken as singular collective. hanū is the dual 'two jaws'.",
